# Forge accounts (git.telpher.stream logins) whose pull requests are certified through the
# project's sign-off ledger instead of a per-commit Signed-off-by: a maintainer reads each
# change on main after it lands and records a signed attestation (see AUTHORSHIP.md).
# One login per line. Read by scripts/dco-check.sh at the pull request's base commit, so a
# pull request cannot add its own account while .gitea/workflows/dco.yml runs unchanged and
# its check is required on the default branch (legal-index's `just protect`, once the kit has landed);
# a pull request that edits that workflow is read for exactly that. Agents commit under these
# accounts and never write a human's sign-off.
